{"id":"mahabharata-13-001","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":1,"title":"प्रथमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 1 · Yudhishthira's grief and the fowler, the serpent and Death","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira says that peace of heart has not come to him after the slaughter. Bhishma tells of the woman Gautami whose son was killed by a serpent, and of the dispute among the hunter, the serpent, Death and Time about who was the cause, and ends with the lesson that no one is guilty alone.","kn":"ಸಂಹಾರದ ನಂತರ ಹೃದಯಕ್ಕೆ ಶಾಂತಿ ಸಿಕ್ಕಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹಾವಿನಿಂದ ಮಗನನ್ನು ಕಳೆದುಕೊಂಡ ಗೌತಮಿ, ಬೇಡ, ಹಾವು, ಮೃತ್ಯು, ಕಾಲರ ವಾದವನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳಿ ಯಾರೂ ಒಬ್ಬರೇ ಅಪರಾಧಿಯಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ತೀರ್ಮಾನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर कहते हैं कि संहार के बाद उनके हृदय को शान्ति नहीं मिली। भीष्म साँप से पुत्र खोने वाली गौतमी और व्याध, सर्प, मृत्यु तथा काल के कारण को लेकर विवाद की कथा सुनाते हैं और निष्कर्ष देते हैं कि कोई अकेला दोषी नहीं।","te":"సంహారం తరువాత తన హృదయానికి శాంతి లభించలేదని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అంటాడు. పాము వల్ల కొడుకును కోల్పోయిన గౌతమి, వేటగాడు, పాము, మృత్యువు, కాలుల మధ్య కారణంపై వాదాన్ని భీష్ముడు చెప్పి ఎవరూ ఒంటరిగా దోషి కారని ముగిస్తాడు.","ta":"போருக்குப் பின் தன் உள்ளத்துக்கு அமைதி கிடைக்கவில்லை என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கூறுகிறார். பாம்பால் மகனை இழந்த கௌதமி, வேடன், பாம்பு, மரணம், காலம் இடையிலான காரண வாதத்தைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறி, யாரும் தனியே குற்றவாளி அல்லர் என்று முடிக்கிறார்.","ml":"കൂട്ടക്കൊലയ്ക്കുശേഷവും തന്റെ മനസ്സിന് സമാധാനമായിട്ടില്ലെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പറയുന്നു. പാമ്പുകടിയേറ്റ് മകൻ മരിച്ച ഗൗതമി എന്ന സ്ത്രീയുടെ കഥ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; വേടൻ, പാമ്പ്, മൃത്യു, കാലം എന്നിവർ ആരാണ് കാരണക്കാരൻ എന്ന തർക്കവും അതിലുണ്ട്. ഒരാൾ മാത്രം കുറ്റക്കാരനല്ലെന്ന പാഠത്തോടെ അത് അവസാനിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.1; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शमो बहुविधाकारः सूक्ष्म उक्तः पितामह ।\nन च मे हृदये शान्तिरस्ति कृत्वेदमीदृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, you have described peace of mind in many subtle forms, yet after doing this deed my heart finds no calm."}},{"n":2,"text":"अस्मिन्नर्थे बहुविधा शान्तिरुक्ता त्वयानघ ।\nस्वकृते का नु शान्तिः स्याच्छमाद्बहुविधादपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Faultless one, you have taught many kinds of peace here; but what peace can there be for one who has himself done the wrong, however many kinds of calm there are?"}},{"n":3,"text":"शराचितशरीरं हि तीव्रव्रणमुदीक्ष्य च ।\nशमं नोपलभे वीर दुष्कृतान्येव चिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your body pierced with arrows and covered in deep wounds, hero, I find no peace, brooding only on the evil I have done."}},{"n":4,"text":"रुधिरेणावसिक्ताङ्गं प्रस्रवन्तं यथाचलम् ।\nत्वां दृष्ट्वा पुरुषव्याघ्र सीदे वर्षास्विवाम्बुजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your limbs are drenched in blood, streaming like a mountain with springs; seeing you, tiger among men, I sink like a lotus in the rains."}},{"n":5,"text":"अतः कष्टतरं किं नु मत्कृते यत्पितामहः ।\nइमामवस्थां गमितः प्रत्यमित्रै रणाजिरे ।\nतथैवान्ये नृपतयः सहपुत्राः सबान्धवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What could be more painful than that, because of me, my grandfather was brought to this state on the battlefield by enemies, as were other kings with their sons and kinsmen?"}},{"n":6,"text":"वयं हि धार्तराष्ट्राश्च कालमन्युवशानुगाः ।\nकृत्वेदं निन्दितं कर्म प्राप्स्यामः कां गतिं नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"We and the sons of Dhritarashtra were all driven by Time and anger; having done this condemned deed, O king, what end shall we reach?"}},{"n":7,"text":"अहं तव ह्यन्तकरः सुहृद्वधकरस्तथा ।\nन शान्तिमधिगच्छामि पश्यंस्त्वां दुःखितं क्षितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have been your destroyer and the killer of my friends; seeing you in pain on the ground, I find no peace."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"परतन्त्रं कथं हेतुमात्मानमनुपश्यसि ।\nकर्मण्यस्मिन्महाभाग सूक्ष्मं ह्येतदतीन्द्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why do you regard yourself as dependent and the cause? In this action, great-souled one, the matter is subtle and beyond the senses."}},{"n":9,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nसंवादं मृत्युगौतम्योः काललुब्धकपन्नगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this point they cite an ancient tale: the dialogue of Death and Gautami with Time, a hunter and a serpent."}},{"n":10,"text":"गौतमी नाम कौन्तेय स्थविरा शमसंयुता ।\nसर्पेण दष्टं स्वं पुत्रमपश्यद्गतचेतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Kunti, there was an old woman named Gautami, serene and self-controlled; she saw her son lifeless, bitten by a snake."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ तं स्नायुपाशेन बद्ध्वा सर्पममर्षितः ।\nलुब्धकोऽर्जुनको नाम गौतम्याः समुपानयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a hunter named Arjunaka, furious, bound the serpent with a cord of sinew and brought it to Gautami."}},{"n":12,"text":"तां चाब्रवीदयं ते स पुत्रहा पन्नगाधमः ।\nब्रूहि क्षिप्रं महाभागे वध्यतां केन हेतुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said to her: \"Here is the vile serpent that killed your son. Tell me quickly, noble lady, how should it be killed?"}},{"n":13,"text":"अग्नौ प्रक्षिप्यतामेष च्छिद्यतां खण्डशोऽपि वा ।\nन ह्ययं बालहा पापश्चिरं जीवितुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Throw it into the fire, or cut it into pieces; this killer of a child is a sinner and does not deserve to live long.\""}},{"text":"गौतम्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Gautami said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"विसृजैनमबुद्धिस्त्वं न वध्योऽर्जुनक त्वया ।\nको ह्यात्मानं गुरुं कुर्यात्प्राप्तव्ये सति चिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Foolish man, let it go; you must not kill it, Arjunaka. Who would burden himself with guilt when what is to be gained lies before him?"}},{"n":15,"text":"प्लवन्ते धर्मलघवो लोकेऽम्भसि यथा प्लवाः ।\nमज्जन्ति पापगुरवः शस्त्रं स्कन्नमिवोदके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those light with merit float in the world like boats on water, while those heavy with sin sink like a dropped weapon in water."}},{"n":16,"text":"न चामृत्युर्भविता वै हतेऽस्मि-\nन्को वात्ययः स्यादहतेऽस्मिञ्जनस्य ।\nअस्योत्सर्गे प्राणयुक्तस्य जन्तो-\nर्मृत्योर्लोकं को नु गच्छेदनन्तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And killing this snake will not undo death; what loss would the world suffer if it is not killed? By freeing a living creature, who would go to the endless realm of Death?"}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"जानाम्येवं नेह गुणागुणज्ञाः\nसर्वे नियुक्ता गुरवो वै भवन्ति ।\nस्वस्थस्यैते तूपदेशा भवन्ति\nतस्मात्क्षुद्रं सर्पमेनं हनिष्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know this: wise, discerning people do not become teachers merely by being appointed; such advice is for the untroubled. Therefore I will kill this petty snake."}},{"n":18,"text":"समीप्सन्तः कालयोगं त्यजन्ति\nसद्यः शुचं त्वर्थविदस्त्यजन्ति ।\nश्रेयः क्षयः शोचतां नित्यशो हि\nतस्मात्त्याज्यं जहि शोकं हतेऽस्मिन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who seek the right moment quickly cast off sorrow; knowers of purpose abandon grief at once. Constant mourning ruins one's good, so give up sorrow and kill this snake."}},{"text":"गौतम्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Gautami said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"न चैवार्तिर्विद्यतेऽस्मद्विधानां\nधर्मारामः सततं सज्जनो हि ।\nनित्यायस्तो बालजनो न चास्ति\nधर्मो ह्येष प्रभवाम्यस्य नाहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"People like us feel no distress, for the good always delight in dharma; only the childish are ever afflicted. This is dharma, and I have no power over it."}},{"n":20,"text":"न ब्राह्मणानां कोपोऽस्ति कुतः कोपाच्च यातना ।\nमार्दवात्क्षम्यतां साधो मुच्यतामेष पन्नगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins feel no anger; and from anger how could torment follow? Out of gentleness, good man, forgive it and set this snake free."}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"हत्वा लाभः श्रेय एवाव्ययं स्या-\nत्सद्यो लाभो बलवद्भिः प्रशस्तः ।\nकालाल्लाभो यस्तु सद्यो भवेत\nहते श्रेयः कुत्सिते त्वीदृशे स्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Killing it would bring lasting good; the strong praise immediate gain, and gain that comes at once at the right time is best. Killing such a despicable creature is good."}},{"text":"गौतम्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Gautami said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"कार्थप्राप्तिर्गृह्य शत्रुं निहत्य\nका वा शान्तिः प्राप्य शत्रुं नमुक्त्वा ।\nकस्मात्सौम्य भुजगे न क्षमेयं\nमोक्षं वा किं कारणं नास्य कुर्याम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What gain is there in seizing and killing an enemy, or what peace in catching him and not releasing him? Gentle man, why should I not forgive the serpent, or why not grant it release?"}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"अस्मादेकस्माद्बहवो रक्षितव्या\nनैको बहुभ्यो गौतमि रक्षितव्यः ।\nकृतागसं धर्मविदस्त्यजन्ति\nसरीसृपं पापमिमं जहि त्वम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many should be protected by sacrificing one; one should not be protected at the expense of many, Gautami. The knowers of dharma abandon an offender; kill this sinful crawler."}},{"text":"गौतम्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Gautami said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"नास्मिन्हते पन्नगे पुत्रको मे\nसंप्राप्स्यते लुब्धक जीवितं वै ।\nगुणं चान्यं नास्य वधे प्रपश्ये\nतस्मात्सर्पं लुब्धक मुञ्च जीवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hunter, my son will not regain life by this serpent's death, and I see no other benefit in killing it; so release the snake alive."}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"वृत्रं हत्वा देवराट्श्रेष्ठभाग्वै\nयज्ञं हत्वा भागमवाप चैव ।\nशूली देवो देववृत्तं कुरु त्वं\nक्षिप्रं सर्पं जहि मा भूद्विशङ्का ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of gods, by killing Vritra, won the best share, and by destroying the sacrifice the trident-bearing god got his portion. Do what the gods did: kill the snake quickly, without doubt."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"असकृत्प्रोच्यमानापि गौतमी भुजगं प्रति ।\nलुब्धकेन महाभागा पापे नैवाकरोन्मतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though the hunter urged her again and again, the noble Gautami never turned her mind to evil against the serpent."}},{"n":27,"text":"ईषदुच्छ्वसमानस्तु कृच्छ्रात्संस्तभ्य पन्नगः ।\nउत्ससर्ज गिरं मन्दां मानुषीं पाशपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the serpent, bound in the noose, breathing faintly, steadied himself with effort and spoke in a weak human voice."}},{"n":28,"text":"को न्वर्जुनक दोषोऽत्र विद्यते मम बालिश ।\nअस्वतन्त्रं हि मां मृत्युर्विवशं यदचूचुदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Foolish Arjunaka, what fault is mine here? Death drove me, helpless and powerless, to do it."}},{"n":29,"text":"तस्यायं वचनाद्दष्टो न कोपेन न काम्यया ।\nतस्य तत्किल्बिषं लुब्ध विद्यते यदि किल्बिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He bit at that one's command, not from anger or desire. If there is any guilt in this, hunter, it is his.\""}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"यद्यन्यवशगेनेदं कृतं ते पन्नगाशुभम् ।\nकारणं वै त्वमप्यत्र तस्मात्त्वमपि किल्बिषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Serpent, if you did this evil under another's control, you are still a cause in it, and so you too are guilty."}},{"n":31,"text":"मृत्पात्रस्य क्रियायां हि दण्डचक्रादयो यथा ।\nकारणत्वे प्रकल्प्यन्ते तथा त्वमपि पन्नग ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the staff and wheel and the rest are counted as causes in making a clay pot, so are you, serpent."}},{"n":32,"text":"किल्बिषी चापि मे वध्यः किल्बिषी चासि पन्नग ।\nआत्मानं कारणं ह्यत्र त्वमाख्यासि भुजंगम ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are guilty and deserve death at my hands, serpent; and you yourself name yourself as a cause here."}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"सर्व एते ह्यस्ववशा दण्डचक्रादयो यथा ।\nतथाहमपि तस्मान्मे नैष हेतुर्मतस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of these, like the staff and wheel, are not independent; so am I. Therefore, I do not accept that I am the cause, as you think."}},{"n":34,"text":"अथ वा मतमेतत्ते तेऽप्यन्योन्यप्रयोजकाः ।\nकार्यकारणसंदेहो भवत्यन्योन्यचोदनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or if you hold that they too each set the others in motion, then doubt arises over what is cause and effect, since each drives the other."}},{"n":35,"text":"एवं सति न दोषो मे नास्मि वध्यो न किल्बिषी ।\nकिल्बिषं समवाये स्यान्मन्यसे यदि किल्बिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That being so, I am not at fault, nor deserving death, nor guilty; if you think guilt arises from the coming together of causes, then it is a shared guilt."}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"कारणं यदि न स्याद्वै न कर्ता स्यास्त्वमप्युत ।\nविनाशे कारणं त्वं च तस्माद्वध्योऽसि मे मतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If there were no cause, you would not be the doer either; yet you are a cause in this destruction, so I judge that you deserve to die."}},{"n":37,"text":"असत्यपि कृते कार्ये नेह पन्नग लिप्यते ।\nतस्मान्नात्रैव हेतुः स्याद्वध्यः किं बहु भाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if an act is not done, serpent, one is not tainted here; so there could be no cause here. Why talk so much? You must die."}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"कार्याभावे क्रिया न स्यात्सत्यसत्यपि कारणे ।\nतस्मात्त्वमस्मिन्हेतौ मे वाच्यो हेतुर्विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without an effect there is no action, even if the cause exists; so you must name the specific cause in my case."}},{"n":39,"text":"यद्यहं कारणत्वेन मतो लुब्धक तत्त्वतः ।\nअन्यः प्रयोगे स्यादत्र किल्बिषी जन्तुनाशने ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I am truly considered the cause, hunter, then another who instigated it would also be guilty in the killing of the creature."}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"वध्यस्त्वं मम दुर्बुद्धे बालघाती नृशंसकृत् ।\nभाषसे किं बहु पुनर्वध्यः सन्पन्नगाधम ॥","meaning":{"en":"You must die, wicked one, killer of a child, doer of cruelty. Why do you say so much, vilest of serpents? You deserve death."}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"यथा हवींषि जुह्वाना मखे वै लुब्धकर्त्विजः ।\nन फलं प्राप्नुवन्त्यत्र परलोके तथा ह्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just as priests offering oblations in a sacrifice, hunter, do not gain the fruit of it in the next world, so it is with me."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":42,"text":"तथा ब्रुवति तस्मिंस्तु पन्नगे मृत्युचोदिते ।\nआजगाम ततो मृत्युः पन्नगं चाब्रवीदिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the serpent, driven by Death, spoke thus, Death himself came and addressed the serpent."}},{"n":43,"text":"कालेनाहं प्रणुदितः पन्नग त्वामचूचुदम् ।\nविनाशहेतुर्नास्य त्वमहं वा प्राणिनः शिशोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Serpent, I was impelled by Time, and I urged you on. Neither you nor I is the cause of this child's destruction."}},{"n":44,"text":"यथा वायुर्जलधरान्विकर्षति ततस्ततः ।\nतद्वज्जलदवत्सर्प कालस्याहं वशानुगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the wind drives clouds here and there, so I, serpent, follow the will of Time, like a cloud."}},{"n":45,"text":"सात्त्विका राजसाश्चैव तामसा ये च केचन ।\nभावाः कालात्मकाः सर्वे प्रवर्तन्ते हि जन्तुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"All states, whether of goodness, passion or darkness, arise in creatures as products of Time."}},{"n":46,"text":"जङ्गमाः स्थावराश्चैव दिवि वा यदि वा भुवि ।\nसर्वे कालात्मकाः सर्प कालात्मकमिदं जगत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All things moving and unmoving, in heaven or on earth, are of the nature of Time, serpent; this whole world is Time's."}},{"n":47,"text":"प्रवृत्तयश्च या लोके तथैव च निवृत्तयः ।\nतासां विकृतयो याश्च सर्वं कालात्मकं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All activities in the world, and likewise all cessations, and their transformations, are said to be of the nature of Time."}},{"n":48,"text":"आदित्यश्चन्द्रमा विष्णुरापो वायुः शतक्रतुः ।\nअग्निः खं पृथिवी मित्र ओषध्यो वसवस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sun, the moon, Vishnu, the waters, the wind, Indra, fire, space, earth, Mitra, the plants and the Vasus,"}},{"n":49,"text":"सरितः सागराश्चैव भावाभावौ च पन्नग ।\nसर्वे कालेन सृज्यन्ते ह्रियन्ते च तथा पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"rivers and oceans, being and non-being, serpent: all are created and taken away again by Time."}},{"n":50,"text":"एवं ज्ञात्वा कथं मां त्वं सदोषं सर्प मन्यसे ।\nअथ चैवंगते दोषो मयि त्वमपि दोषवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this, why do you think me at fault? And if that were so, you too would be at fault.\""}},{"text":"सर्प उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The serpent said:"}},{"n":51,"text":"निर्दोषं दोषवन्तं वा न त्वा मृत्यो ब्रवीम्यहम् ।\nत्वयाहं चोदित इति ब्रवीम्येतावदेव तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Death, I call you neither faultless nor at fault; I say only this, that I was driven by you."}},{"n":52,"text":"यदि काले तु दोषोऽस्ति यदि तत्रापि नेष्यते ।\nदोषो नैव परीक्ष्यो मे न ह्यत्राधिकृता वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If fault lies with Time, and that too is not accepted, then I need not be examined for fault, for we have no authority here."}},{"n":53,"text":"निर्मोक्षस्त्वस्य दोषस्य मया कार्यो यथा तथा ।\nमृत्यो विदोषः स्यामेव यथा तन्मे प्रयोजनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I must somehow secure release from this charge; Death, let me be free of fault, as that is my purpose."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":54,"text":"सर्पोऽथार्जुनकं प्राह श्रुतं ते मृत्युभाषितम् ।\nनानागसं मां पाशेन संतापयितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the serpent said to Arjunaka, \"You have heard Death's words. You should not torment me with the noose, for I am blameless.\""}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":55,"text":"मृत्योः श्रुतं मे वचनं तव चैव भुजंगम ।\nनैव तावद्विदोषत्वं भवति त्वयि पन्नग ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have heard the words of Death and yours, serpent, but that does not yet make you faultless."}},{"n":56,"text":"मृत्युस्त्वं चैव हेतुर्हि जन्तोरस्य विनाशने ।\nउभयं कारणं मन्ये न कारणमकारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You and Death are both causes in the destruction of this creature; I consider both to be causes, and the absence of cause is no cause."}},{"n":57,"text":"धिङ्मृत्युं च दुरात्मानं क्रूरं दुःखकरं सताम् ।\nत्वां चैवाहं वधिष्यामि पापं पापस्य कारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shame on Death, the wicked, cruel causer of grief to the good; and I will kill you too, sinful one, the cause of a sinful deed."}},{"text":"मृत्युरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Death said:"}},{"n":58,"text":"विवशौ कालवशगावावां तद्दिष्टकारिणौ ।\nनावां दोषेण गन्तव्यौ यदि सम्यक्प्रपश्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"We two are helpless, subject to Time, doing what he decrees. If you see rightly, you should not blame us."}},{"text":"लुब्धक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":59,"text":"युवामुभौ कालवशौ यदि वै मृत्युपन्नगौ ।\nहर्षक्रोधौ कथं स्यातामेतदिच्छामि वेदितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you, Death and serpent, are both under Time's control, I want to know how joy and anger can arise in you."}},{"text":"मृत्युरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Death said:"}},{"n":60,"text":"याः काश्चिदिह चेष्टाः स्युः सर्वाः कालप्रचोदिताः ।\nपूर्वमेवैतदुक्तं हि मया लुब्धक कालतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever actions occur here are all driven by Time; I have already told you this, hunter, in speaking of Time."}},{"n":61,"text":"तस्मादुभौ कालवशावावां तद्दिष्टकारिणौ ।\nनावां दोषेण गन्तव्यौ त्वया लुब्धक कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So we two are subject to Time, doing what he ordains; you should never judge us at fault, hunter."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":62,"text":"अथोपगम्य कालस्तु तस्मिन्धर्मार्थसंशये ।\nअब्रवीत्पन्नगं मृत्युं लुब्धमर्जुनकं च तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Time himself approached, in that doubt over dharma and purpose, and spoke to the serpent, Death, and the hunter Arjunaka."}},{"text":"काल उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Time said:"}},{"n":63,"text":"नैवाहं नाप्ययं मृत्युर्नायं लुब्धक पन्नगः ।\nकिल्बिषी जन्तुमरणे न वयं हि प्रयोजकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither I, nor Death, nor this serpent, hunter, is guilty in the death of a creature; we are not the instigators."}},{"n":64,"text":"अकरोद्यदयं कर्म तन्नोऽर्जुनक चोदकम् ।\nप्रणाशहेतुर्नान्योऽस्य वध्यतेऽयं स्वकर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was the child's own deed that urged us on, Arjunaka; there is no other cause of its destruction. It is killed by its own karma."}},{"n":65,"text":"यदनेन कृतं कर्म तेनायं निधनं गतः ।\nविनाशहेतुः कर्मास्य सर्वे कर्मवशा वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the deed he did, this child met his end; his own karma is the cause of his destruction. We are all subject to karma."}},{"n":66,"text":"कर्मदायादवाँल्लोकः कर्मसंबन्धलक्षणः ।\nकर्माणि चोदयन्तीह यथान्योन्यं तथा वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The world is heir to its deeds and is marked by their bonds; deeds drive one another here, and so do we."}},{"n":67,"text":"यथा मृत्पिण्डतः कर्ता कुरुते यद्यदिच्छति ।\nएवमात्मकृतं कर्म मानवः प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a potter makes whatever he wishes from a lump of clay, so a human reaps the deed he himself has done."}},{"n":68,"text":"यथा छायातपौ नित्यं सुसंबद्धौ निरन्तरम् ।\nतथा कर्म च कर्ता च संबद्धावात्मकर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As shade and sunlight are always closely joined, so are deed and doer bound together by their own actions."}},{"n":69,"text":"एवं नाहं न वै मृत्युर्न सर्पो न तथा भवान् ।\nन चेयं ब्राह्मणी वृद्धा शिशुरेवात्र कारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So neither I, nor Death, nor the serpent, nor you, nor this aged brahmin woman is the cause here; the child himself is."}},{"n":70,"text":"तस्मिंस्तथा ब्रुवाणे तु ब्राह्मणी गौतमी नृप ।\nस्वकर्मप्रत्ययाँल्लोकान्मत्वार्जुनकमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Time spoke thus, the brahmin woman Gautami, O king, concluded that people reap what their own deeds bring, and said to Arjunaka:"}},{"n":71,"text":"नैव कालो न भुजगो न मृत्युरिह कारणम् ।\nस्वकर्मभिरयं बालः कालेन निधनं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Neither Time, nor the serpent, nor Death is the cause here; this boy died in Time's course through his own deeds."}},{"n":72,"text":"मया च तत्कृतं कर्म येनायं मे मृतः सुतः ।\nयातु कालस्तथा मृत्युर्मुञ्चार्जुनक पन्नगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I too did the deed by which my son died. Let Time and Death go; Arjunaka, release the serpent.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":73,"text":"ततो यथागतं जग्मुर्मृत्युः कालोऽथ पन्नगः ।\nअभूद्विरोषोऽर्जुनको विशोका चैव गौतमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Death, Time and the serpent went as they had come; Arjunaka was freed from anger and Gautami from grief."}},{"n":74,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा शमं गच्छ मा भूश्चिन्तापरो नृप ।\nस्वकर्मप्रत्ययाँल्लोकांस्त्रीन्विद्धि मनुजर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, find peace and do not be absorbed in worry, O king; know that the three worlds depend on their own deeds."}},{"n":75,"text":"न तु त्वया कृतं पार्थ नापि दुर्योधनेन वै ।\nकालेन तत्कृतं विद्धि विहता येन पार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not you, son of Pritha, nor Duryodhana did it; know that Time did it, by whom the kings were destroyed."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":76,"text":"इत्येतद्वचनं श्रुत्वा बभूव विगतज्वरः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरो महातेजाः पप्रच्छेदं च धर्मवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words, the radiant Yudhishthira, who knew dharma, was freed from his fever of grief and asked this question."}}]}]}